  "content": {
    "id": "p29-q25-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "25",
    "prompt": "The dimensions of a cuboid are $a\\text{ cm}\\times b\\text{ cm}\\times c\\text{ cm}$, where $a$, $b$ and $c$ are positive integers satisfying $a<b<c$. The surface area of the cuboid is $52\\text{ cm}^2$. Find $(a,b,c)$. Note: There are two possible answers.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p29-q25-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "(1,2,8)\\text{ or }(2,3,4)",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p29-q25-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "ab+ac+bc=26",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and consider the cases ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "a=1",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "a=2",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2ab+2ac+2bc&=52\\\\ab+ac+bc&=26\\end{align*}$$\nIf $a\\ge3$, then $b\\ge4$ and $c\\ge5$, so $ab+ac+bc\\ge12+15+20=47$. Thus $a=1$ or $a=2$.\n\nFor $a=1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}b+c+bc&=26\\\\(b+1)(c+1)&=27\\end{align*}$$\nThe factor pair satisfying $1<b<c$ is $3\\times9$, giving $b=2$ and $c=8$.\n\nFor $a=2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2b+2c+bc&=26\\\\(b+2)(c+2)&=30\\end{align*}$$\nThe factor pair satisfying $2<b<c$ is $5\\times6$, giving $b=3$ and $c=4$.\n\nTherefore $(a,b,c)=(1,2,8)$ or $(2,3,4)$.",
